    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA Home Rich in Character, History & Endless Potential\n\nNestled amidst the tranquil countryside of Ballyeden, Davidstown, this charming three bedroom detached residence is a home that tells a story. Lovingly cared for by generations, it is filled with warmth, character and cherished memories, offering a rare opportunity for its next owners to breathe new life into a truly special property.\n\nOccupying an 0.64 acre site, the property enjoys a peaceful rural setting surrounded by rolling countryside, where natural light floods the property throughout the day and the changing seasons provide a beautiful backdrop from every window. While the interior proudly reflects its heritage, showcasing features and the distinctive charm of a traditional Irish family home, it also presents an exciting blank canvas for those wishing to create a contemporary country residence while preserving its authentic character.\n\nThe accommodation extends to approximately 70sq.m. and comprises three bedrooms, comfortable living accommodation, a kitchen, bathroom and reception space, all offering wonderful scope for modernisation and personalisation. Every room possesses its own unique personality, a quality that is becoming increasingly rare in today's market, making this property as memorable as it is inviting.\n\nOutside, the generous site provides endless possibilities. Whether you dream of landscaped gardens, a productive vegetable plot, a family play area or simply a peaceful place to enjoy the surrounding countryside, there is ample space to bring your vision to life. A detached garage and additional outdoor storage buildings further enhance the property's practicality, providing excellent space for hobbies, workshops or future adaptation, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\n\nBallyeden enjoys the perfect balance of peaceful country living and everyday convenience. Davidstown is a welcoming rural community renowned for its scenic surroundings, local national school, church and GAA club, while the bustling market town of Enniscorthy is just a 13 minute drive away via N30, offering an excellent selection of shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, schools and leisure amenities and Wexford Town approx. 27 minute drive away via R730. The nearby N30, N25 & M11 provides an easy commute to New Ross, Waterford, Gorey and Dublin.\n\nOffering charm, privacy, generous grounds and exceptional potential, this is more than simply a house - it is an opportunity to create a forever home while becoming part of its continuing story. Whether you are searching for a peaceful countryside retreat, a family home to make your own, or a rewarding renovation project, Ballyeden presents an opportunity that is as exciting as it is unique.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the setting, character and endless possibilities this delightful property has to offer."
      },
